{
  "_about": "Ledger CSV canonical layer - the four portal ledger downloads (Electronic Cash Ledger, Electronic Credit Ledger, Electronic Liability Register = Part I, Electronic Liability Ledger = Part II / DRC) (spec: docs/LEDGER_CANONICAL_SPEC.md). Each is a CSV with a title, a few GSTIN/From/To lines, a two-row heading (group heading row + sub-heading row, the row starting 'Sr.No') and one row per transaction, an 'Opening Balance' row and a 'Closing Balance' row. The original took every column by FIXED POSITION ('pos', unchanged). The converter also reads the headings: 'label' = fragments that must all appear in the column's heading (compared after lower-casing and stripping non-alphanumerics); for the amount columns 'group' = fragments of the group heading above (a group heading spans its six columns Tax / Interest / Penalty / Fee / Others / Total) and 'sub' = the sub-heading, which must equal; 'nth' (credit ledger) = which of the columns carrying that sub-heading (1 = Credit/Debit block, 2 = Balance block). A field is taken from 'pos' if its heading matches; if not, from the one other unused column whose heading matches (warning W902); if none, from 'pos' anyway as the original did (warning W901). 'type': 'num' = number (blank / '-' = 0; Indian '3,06,53,037.00' grouping fine), 'raw' = kept as text. 'required': true = the file is rejected (E903) if the column cannot be located. 'min_width' = a row narrower than this is not a transaction row. Field names: amt_<head>_<part> = the Debited/Credited block, bal_<head>_<part> = the Balance block; head = igst/cgst/sgst/cess; part = tax/interest/penalty/fee/others/total.",
